# This file is committed on purpose. It holds public configuration only.
#
# Anything that should NOT be in the repo goes in `.env.local` instead —
# that's gitignored (`.env*.local`), and @expo/env loads it *ahead* of this
# file, so a value set there wins without editing anything tracked.
#
# The one variable that would otherwise land here by mistake is
# EXPO_PUBLIC_VERDICT_TOKEN (see the Auth section in worker/README.md).
# Put it in `.env.local`.
#
# Be clear-eyed about what that buys, though: every EXPO_PUBLIC_* value is
# inlined into the app bundle at build time, so `.env.local` keeps a value
# out of version control and nothing more — it is not secret from anyone
# holding the app. Genuine secrets never reach this project at all: the
# Anthropic API key lives only in Cloudflare, set via `wrangler secret put`.

# Points the app at the deployed verdicts service (see worker/ and
# docs/deferred-work.md). Not a secret — it's just a public URL; the actual
# secret (the Anthropic API key) lives only in Cloudflare, never here.
# Unset this (or delete the file) to make the app behave exactly as it did
# before this service existed — see src/lib/verdicts.ts.
EXPO_PUBLIC_VERDICT_URL=https://nofrills-verdicts.richard-coil40.workers.dev

# Points the app at the same Worker for the league catalog (GET /v1/leagues).
# Same base URL as above and the same service — kept as its own variable so
# the two can be switched independently: a build can take verdicts without
# the hosted catalog, or the other way round.
# Unset this and the app runs on the league list bundled into the build,
# touching the network for it not at all — see src/lib/league-catalog.ts.
EXPO_PUBLIC_CATALOG_URL=https://nofrills-verdicts.richard-coil40.workers.dev
